From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:48:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MANIFEST.in: include tests/ in the sdist

Upstream's own pyproject.toml cibuildwheel config
(`before-test = ["pip install -r {project}/tests/requirements.txt"]`,
`test-command = "python -m unittest discover {project}/tests/"`) assumes the
tests/ tree is present next to the built package. That's true when
cibuildwheel runs directly against a git checkout, but MANIFEST.in never
adds tests/requirements.txt or tests/data/ to the sdist (only the top-level
tests/test*.py files land there via setuptools' sdist defaults), so building
wheels from the sdist (as this port does, to build the architecture-independent
sdist once instead of once per riscv64 matrix leg) fails before-test with
"No such file or directory: tests/requirements.txt", and several suites
(test_lp.py, test_serialization_cqm.py, ...) need the data files under
tests/data/. Confirmed the published PyPI sdist for 0.12.22 has the same gap.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; needs a dimod maintainer decision on whether tests/ belongs in the sdist or their own CI should build from a checkout instead]
---
 MANIFEST.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/MANIFEST.in b/MANIFEST.in
index a839c74..dcb4db2 100644
--- a/MANIFEST.in
+++ b/MANIFEST.in
@@ -3,3 +3,4 @@ recursive-include dimod/include *h
 recursive-include dimod *.pyx *.pxd *.pxi *.pyx.src
 include dimod/py.typed
 graft extern/filereaderlp
+recursive-include tests *
